{"id": "EUVD-2026-96552", "enisaUuid": "4d6875bf-7134-3898-a7c1-d4ca26a461b5", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the AiragAppController release handler that allows any authenticated user to publish or unpublish other users' AI applications. Low-privileged attackers can send POST requests to /airag/app/release to obtain share tokens exposing applications to anonymous chat access, or invalidate existing share links.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T02:30:07", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_airag_app_release.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-boot-module/jeecg-boot-module-airag/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/airag/app/controller/AiragAppController.java#L135-L164", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-airag-app-release-endpoint"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5wwp-r26m-h74c", "CVE-2026-108613"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07f33022-5abd-3c4f-8b09-91f52923dead", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a1abafd3-38fb-3d6a-995c-9a05d2d923ba", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}